      "message": "fix(app): the posed first-traverse verdict names the user's heights\n\nMain's posed law (#3084, #3100, #3142) reads a 3+2 plane along the\nframe's axis from its origin, so its verdict carries local heights.\nIt now goes through in_user_frame (pub(super)) before it replaces the\nlower first-traverse verdicts. Without it, the retain compared a local\ntop with the 3+2 law's top in the user frame. Its table verdict also\ntakes the new `tilted` field, so the branch builds on main.\n\nMain's posed pins move by the origin Z (20):\n- first_traverse_table: a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work\n  reads 40 and sqrt(2200) - 20 cos 30 + 20, tilted.\n- first_traverse_table_tilt: the A 30 refusal reads 36 and 38.735,\n  tilted; the plain-script top takes the same shift.\n\nRefs #2991\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
